-- title:
--   Cyclic kernel versus primitivity of the idele g
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $\kappa$-points killed by $q'$ are trivial. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$ and, for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_\mathbb{Q}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_\mathbb{Q}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule that is an order (containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning, finitely generated) and maximal among orders containing it, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring `rationalEndSubring` $\kappa\,X_1$ of $\operatorname{End}$ of the points of $X_1$ generated by the rationally represented additive maps, with image exactly $\Lambda_1$. Fix a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_\mathbb{Q}\mathbb{A}^{\mathrm{fin}}_\mathbb{Q}$, an elliptic curve $W$ over $\kappa$, a nonzero $\chi\colon X_1\to W$ in `rationalHomSet`, and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta_1$ carries the set of maps $\rho\circ\chi$ with $\rho\colon W\to X_1$ rational onto the image under quaternion conjugation of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap x\,\widehat{\Lambda_1})$, where $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ denotes [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$ and the intersection is [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19). Let $g$ be a unit of the same adelic algebra lying in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$, let $W'$ be an elliptic curve over $\kappa$, and let $\psi\colon W\to W'$ and $\psi'\colon W'\to W$ be rational additive maps with $\psi'\circ\psi$ and $\psi\circ\psi'$ both equal to multiplication by $n=\#\ker\psi$, and assume $\theta_1$ carries the set of maps $\rho\circ(\psi\circ\chi)$ with $\rho\colon W'\to X_1$ rational onto the conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\cap xg\,\widehat{\Lambda_1})$. Then $\ker\psi$ is cyclic if and only if $\ell^{-1}g\notin\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ for every prime $\ell$.
--
--   This is the cyclicity half of the Deuring-type dictionary between kernel ideals of a supersingular elliptic curve over $\kappa$ and finite ideles of the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$: the elementary divisors of $g$ at each prime read off the group structure of the kernel of the corresponding isogeny, cyclicity corresponding to primitivity of $g$ in $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_equiv_ofFiniteIdele_mul_isAddCyclic_forall_ker_eq_of_kernelIdealSet_comp_eq), which produces isogenies with prescribed cyclic kernels from such ideles.
